High Value Keywords for Secure Code Review
1. Hardcoded Secrets / Sensitive Data

Search:

password
passwd
secret
apikey
api_key
token
bearer
authorization
auth
privatekey
clientsecret
accesskey
jwt
credential
username
pwd

Look for:

hardcoded credentials
API tokens
JWT secrets
AWS keys

Example vulnerable code:

String password = "admin123";
2. SQL Injection

Search:

executeQuery
execute
createQuery
prepareStatement
Statement
nativeQuery
SELECT
INSERT
UPDATE
DELETE
jdbcTemplate
EntityManager

Dangerous pattern:

"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=" + userInput

Safe:

PreparedStatement
parameterized queries
3. Command Injection

Search:

Runtime.getRuntime
ProcessBuilder
exec(
bash
cmd.exe
powershell
sh -

Dangerous:

Runtime.getRuntime().exec(userInput);
4. Path Traversal / File Read

Search:

File
FileInputStream
Paths.get
getCanonicalPath
MultipartFile
upload
download
readAllBytes
new File(

Dangerous:

new File("/uploads/" + filename)
5. SSRF (Server Side Request Forgery)

Search:

URL(
HttpURLConnection
RestTemplate
WebClient
OkHttpClient
openConnection
http://
https://

Dangerous:

new URL(userInput)
6. XSS (Cross Site Scripting)

Search:

innerHTML
response.getWriter
print(
println(
th:text
th:utext
model.addAttribute
setAttribute

Dangerous:

response.getWriter().print(userInput);
7. Authentication / Authorization Issues

Search:

isAdmin
hasRole
hasAuthority
permitAll
authenticated
authorize
securityConfig
@PreAuthorize
@RolesAllowed

Dangerous:

missing authorization checks
permitAll() on sensitive APIs
8. JWT / Session Weaknesses

Search:

JWT
jwt
signWith
setSigningKey
HS256
session
cookie
JSESSIONID
rememberMe

Check:

weak secrets
no expiration
insecure cookies
9. Debug / Sensitive Logging

Search:

log.info
log.debug
System.out.println
printStackTrace
Exception
logger.error

Dangerous:

log.info("Password: " + password);
10. Deserialization Vulnerabilities

Search:

ObjectInputStream
readObject
deserialize
SerializationUtils
XMLDecoder
Yaml.load
SnakeYAML

High risk if user-controlled input exists.

11. XML Vulnerabilities (XXE)

Search:

DocumentBuilderFactory
SAXParserFactory
XMLInputFactory
Unmarshaller
TransformerFactory

Check if secure processing enabled.

Dangerous if missing:

factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
12. Cryptography Weaknesses

Search:

MD5
SHA1
DES
ECB
SecureRandom
Cipher.getInstance
Base64
encrypt
decrypt

Weak examples:

MD5
SHA1
DES
AES/ECB
13. Open Redirect

Search:

sendRedirect
redirect:
location.href
window.location

Dangerous:

response.sendRedirect(url);
14. CORS Misconfiguration

Search:

@CrossOrigin
Access-Control-Allow-Origin
CorsConfiguration
allowedOrigins

Dangerous:

allowedOrigins("*")
15. File Upload Vulnerabilities

Search:

MultipartFile
upload
transferTo
getOriginalFilename
contentType

Check:

extension validation
MIME validation
path traversal
16. Insecure Randomness

Search:

Random()
Math.random
UUID.randomUUID

For security tokens:

use SecureRandom
